Display Dictionary Elements
---------------------------
Method 1: Printing the Entire Collection Structure.
      emps = {101: 'Vishnu', 102: 'Akash';, 103: 'Naveen'}
      print(emps)
      # Output: {101: 'Vishnu', 102: 'Akash';, 103: 'Naveen'}

Method 2: Display specific element by using key.
      emps = {101: 'Vishnu', 102: 'Akash';, 103: 'Naveen'}
      print(emps[101]) #Vishnu

Method 3: Display one by one using for loop.
      1)Only keys
      sData={"Akash":'73733773',"Prakash":"23224222"}
      for i in (sData.keys()):
          print(i)
      Output
      ------
      Akash
      Prakash

          OR
      sData={"Akash":'73733773',"Prakash":"23224222"}
      for i in (sData):
          print(i)
      Output
      ------
      Akash
      Prakash

      2)Only values
      --------------
      sData={"Akash":'73733773',"Prakash":"23224222"}
      for i in (sData.values()):
          print(i)
      Output
      ------
      73733773
      23224222

      3)Key and value
      ---------------
      sData={"Akash":'73733773',"Prakash":"23224222"}
      for i,j in (sData.items()):
          print(i,j)
      Output
      ------
      Akash 73733773
      Prakash 23224222

