Built-in functions
-------------------
d = {"a": 1, "b": 2, "c": 3}

1)len(d) #3 -Returns number of key-value pairs
2)type(d) #<class 'dict'> - Returns the type of object
3)str(d) # "{'a': 1, 'b': 2, 'c': 3}" - Converts dictionary to string format.
4)dict() # {} - Creates a new empty dictionary
5)max(d) # 'c' - Returns the largest key (based on ASCII/lexicographic order)
6)min(d) # 'a' - Returns the smallest key
7)sorted(d) # ['a', 'b', 'c'] - Returns sorted list of keys
8)sum(d.values()) #6 -sum of all values

